
  NUMERATOR + DENOMINATOR = THE NUMBER ITSELF

======================================================================

  The Cayley address of n: x_n = (n-1)/(n+1)

  In reduced form (a/b with gcd(a,b)=1):
  If n is even: gcd(n-1, n+1) = 1 (both odd). Address = (n-1)/(n+1).
  If n is odd:  gcd(n-1, n+1) = 2 (both even). Address = (n-1)/2 / (n+1)/2.

  n    address     reduced      a    b    a+b    a+b = n?
